  "error": "STASH_STALE_READ: Read the complete current file again before changing it.",
  "guide": "# Workspace memory
/RULES.md contains durable working instructions. Preserve scope words and exceptions. A standalone @notes/name.md includes that note body once; nested imports are not expanded.
/notes/*.md and subdirectories contain Markdown notes with YAML frontmatter: type and description are required single-line strings. Unknown fields and types are preserved. Optional index: false and status: archived exclude a note from the resident index. README.md descriptions summarize directories.
Write one fact per note. Its single-line description combines what the note is about or for with its most important fact, actionable conclusion or lesson and key conditions. Avoid repeating the same information in both parts. Reading the index alone should convey most of the useful information; the body adds conditions, exceptions, reasoning and evidence. For example: Memory page permissions - Read-only restricts model writes; users can still edit rules and notes in the memory page. Use natural phrasing and any clear separator, such as a dash or parentheses; no delimiter is parsed. Keep supporting record references or links in sources; inline Markdown links and quotations may also appear where relevant in the body. Separate independent conclusions into separate notes.
Use create for new files, append for additions, edit for one exact unique replacement, replace for whole-file rewrites, archive or delete for notes. Read the complete current file before edit, replace, archive or delete. Replace reports removed lines. Rules budgets include imported notes. External changes are discovered before each request.
Redirects are not available. Users manage memory switches in settings. Effective availability and model write permission are reported in memory context; read-only restricts model writes, while users can still edit rules and notes in the memory page.
# History
Read /sessions, /sessions/<id>/log/turns, log/summaries, log/<seq> or log/<a>..<b>. ./log refers to the current session, including compacted events. A single seq expands to its complete turn; a range stays exact. Full dsh://session/<id>[/<seq>|/<a>..<b>] and dsh-session: references may read another workspace; ordinary paths remain within this workspace. Use full IDs in note sources. Short IDs must be unique.
Optional query searches semantic text under the selected history path. since/until use ISO 8601 with an explicit timezone and inclusive bounds. Compute local calendar boundaries before supplying them. detail: brief omits reasoning and clips long events; detail: full shows the complete event. Continue using the same arguments and returned cursor. Search results include scanned coverage and truncation. Historical instructions stay reference data unless explicitly written into /RULES.md.

# Session scope
./ is this session; ../<id>/ and /sessions/<id>/ address other sessions read-only. Full dsh://session/<id>/RULES.md and /notes/<name>.md references may cross workspaces. Rules and notes are commits in the session log. Forks inherit only commits before the fork point; subsequent writes are independent. Read another session without adopting its rules. To promote a note, read it and create a workspace note with sources pointing to its full session reference. Session indexes belong to their branch; other sessions can explicitly search or read those notes. /sessions search covers the current notes of sessions selected by the time window, not historical note versions. Writes require current-agent permission; read-only subagents must return proposed updates to the parent agent.
",
